{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":293177,"duration_api_ms":398054,"num_turns":30,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"48d76252-0327-4bc3-9240-990f60a4212a","total_cost_usd":1.8337309499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":4509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79143,"cache_read_input_tokens":1216878,"output_tokens":10073,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4509,"outputTokens":10073,"cacheReadInputTokens":1216878,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79143,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.37745275,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2386,"outputTokens":16121,"cacheReadInputTokens":1860997,"cacheCreationInputTokens":149750,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4562782,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `root_oxygenation_active_biomass_g()` (substrate.rs:140), `compute_habitat_registry(state)` recomputes the full habitat registry from scratch on every call. Within the engine tick loop, `step_substrate_zones()` is called after `refresh_habitat_registry()` has already updated `state.habitat_registry`. Consider accepting the registry as a parameter or using `state.habitat_registry` directly within the hot path, and only falling back to recomputation in the standalone `root_oxygenation_bonus_cm()` public accessor which may be called with stale state from tracing/test code.","rationale":"This is a per-tick performance concern. `compute_habitat_registry` iterates all substrate layers, habitats, and plant guilds. Calling it redundantly every tick adds unnecessary overhead in the engine step loop, especially as the number of habitats/layers grows. Not a correctness bug, but a measurable inefficiency on the hot path."},{"body":"The comment block for integration test `planted_substrate_denitrification_interaction` (root_zone_oxygenation.rs:131-133) states 'planted substrate shows more N₂ export from denitrification (deeper oxic zone → larger suboxic zone pushed deeper → more capacity)'. This reasoning is incorrect: deeper oxic zone means *less* suboxic volume, leading to *less* denitrification per hour, as correctly demonstrated by `root_oxygenation_reduces_hourly_denitrification_when_it_shrinks_suboxic_volume` (line 168). The test assertion itself only checks for divergence (abs difference > 0.001) which is correct, but the comment misattributes the direction of the effect and could mislead future developers.","rationale":"Misleading scientific comments in test code create maintenance risk. A future developer reading this comment would expect rooted plants to increase denitrification, which contradicts the model's actual behavior (deeper oxic zone reduces suboxic volume and thus denitrification capacity). The comment should describe the mechanism correctly: rooted oxygenation changes the O₂ profile, shifting denitrification capacity in either direction depending on substrate depth and base penetration."}],"summary":"The root-zone oxygenation (ROL) implementation is solid and meets all acceptance criteria. The Bouldin diffusion model with exponential-saturating ROL bonus is mathematically correct — the bonus is bounded by remaining substrate depth, preventing overshoot without needing an explicit clamp. Guild filtering correctly restricts ROL to RootFeedingRosette only. The `rol_rate_cm_per_g` parameter is properly exposed as a named, configurable TOML field with serde defaults and invariant validation. Test coverage is comprehensive: 7 unit tests + 5 integration tests covering planted vs. unplanted divergence, proportional biomass response with diminishing returns, floating plant exclusion, zero-biomass edge case, parameter sensitivity, and full tracing/budget exposure. All 12 tests pass. Two minor issues found: (1) redundant habitat registry recomputation on the hot path, and (2) a misleading comment in one integration test that incorrectly describes the expected direction of the denitrification effect."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e3feb7e5-388b-402d-99c2-e52073088c01"}
